---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — CloudOps Guard"
  description="A truthful description of what this website's current implementation does and does not do with data, as of Phase 3H -- before any production deployment."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="status-label status-label--neutral">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        This page describes what this website's implementation actually does today. It is not a legal
        privacy policy, and it makes no promise beyond what is described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Interactive demonstrations</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/demo/kubernetes">Kubernetes</a> and <a href="/demo/gitlab">GitLab</a> demonstration
        pages use fixed, synthetic example data for a fictional project. This data is not real; it does
        not describe any actual cluster, GitLab project, person, or organization.
      </p>

      <h2>The local report explorer</h2>
      <p>
        A <code>report.json</code> file you select in the <a href="/explorer">local report explorer</a> is
        read and rendered entirely in your browser tab. See <a href="/learn/local-report-privacy"
          >how the local report explorer keeps your report private</a
        > for the exact mechanics.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No analytics, session replay, or third-party tracking script runs on any page.</li>
        <li>No endpoint on this site accepts an uploaded report, file, or credential.</li>
        <li>No contact or feedback form exists on this site yet.</li>
        <li>No production deployment of this v0.3.0 website has occurred.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content-Security-Policy</h2>
      <p>
        The routes that can hold report-derived data &mdash; <a href="/demo/kubernetes">/demo/kubernetes</a>, <a href="/demo/gitlab">/demo/gitlab</a>, and <a href="/explorer">/explorer</a> &mdash; are served with a restrictive Content-Security-Policy, including <code>connect-src 'none'</code>, as a browser-enforced backstop against any network request those pages' code might otherwise issue.
      </p>

      <p><a href="/roadmap">See the roadmap</a> for what is planned or still absent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
